    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Memoir by Carlo Henze, M.D. (1907-2003) concerning his service in WWII: As a medical doctor specializing in pharmacology and a native German speaker, Henze served as a Captain in the U.S. Army Medical Corps. He was assigned as a medical intelligence officer to the top-secret Alsos Mission in Europe, whose goal was to determine German progress in developing an atomic bomb and biological and chemical weapons.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
